<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Autopage year share up, div doubles.</title>
<headline>Autopage year share up, div doubles.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended February 28</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     10.6	  vs 6.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 4.0	   vs 2.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   3.84	  vs 2.34</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   7.97	  vs 5.64</p>
<p>    Tax			 3.17	  vs 2.41</p>
<p>    Interest recieved     3.05	  vs 0.05</p>
<p>    Turnover		  250.42	vs 209.30</p>
<p>Div payable June 2</p>
<p>on register May 23</p>
<p>Full name: Autopage Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Phones to pagers firm Autopage said the group had completed its rationalisation and was ready to take advantage of emerging opportunities in the wireless communications sector through organic growth and suitable acquisitions.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
